WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.580
AI systems need logging and monitoring to operate safely.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:18.360
Teams often need visibility into errors, latency, model usage, retrieval failures, tool failures, rate limits, policy events, abuse signals, configuration changes, and unusual activity.

3
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:26.300
Without observability, it is difficult to troubleshoot reliability problems, detect incidents, or prove that controls are working.

4
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.820
Monitoring does not always require full prompt and response content.

5
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:44.120
Many operational goals can be met with metadata such as tenant ID, request size, model route, status code, latency, token counts, policy category, retrieval source identifier, or error type.

6
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:55.500
When content capture is necessary, teams should define a narrow purpose, limit the scope, redact sensitive fields, set short retention, and restrict who can view the logs.

7
00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.180
Observability systems deserve the same governance as the primary application.

8
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:10.360
Log aggregation tools, metrics platforms, tracing systems, alert payloads, and incident tickets can all contain prompt history or sensitive fragments.

9
00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:18.940
Secrets, credentials, personal data, customer data, and regulated content should be filtered where practical before they enter logs.

10
00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:28.240
Access to observability data should be role-based, audited, and reviewed because logs often become one of the broadest internal data sources.

11
00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.360
Incident response should be prepared before a sensitive capture occurs.

12
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:53.500
If prompt history is exposed, over-collected, retained too long, or copied into the wrong system, responders need to identify affected systems, restrict access, preserve audit evidence, coordinate security and privacy review, remove or expire data where appropriate, and adjust controls to prevent recurrence.

13
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.200
Good logging is not the same as collecting everything.

14
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:03.380
It is collecting what the team needs, protecting it well, and knowing how to respond when the record lifecycle goes wrong.
